<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fondaco dei Tedeschi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fondaco dei Tedeschi is a large building beside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rialto">Rialto</a> Bridge in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> that served from the 13th century as the headquarters, warehouse and lodging of German merchants, who were required to live and trade there under Venetian supervision. After a fire it was rebuilt in 1505–1508, with exterior frescoes by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giorgione">Giorgione</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/titian">Titian</a>. It symbolised Venice's role as intermediary between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> and central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fondaco-dei-tedeschi.jpg" alt="Fondaco dei Tedeschi" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Didier Descouens · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fondaco_dei_Tedeschi_2012-05-13.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
